manganic.en:
a. Of, pertaining to resembling, or containing, manganese;
   specif., designating compounds in which manganese has a higher valence
   as contrasted with manganous compounds. Cf. Manganous.

matronize.en:
v. t. To make a matron of; to make matronlike.
v. t. To act the part of a marton toward; to superintend;
   to chaperone; as, to matronize an assembly.

meconic.en:
a. Pertaining to, or obtained from, the poppy or opium;
   specif. (Chem.), designating an acid related to aconitic acid, found in
   opium and extracted as a white crystalline substance.

meiny.en:
n. A family, including servants, etc.; household; retinue;
   train.
n. Company; band; army.

mephistophelian.en:
a. Pertaining to, or resembling, the devil
   Mephistopheles, "a crafty, scoffing, relentless fiend;" devilish;
   crafty.

milliary.en:
a. Of or pertaining to a mile, or to distance by miles;
   denoting a mile or miles.
a. A milestone.

mineralizer.en:
n. An element which is combined with a metal, thus
   forming an ore. Thus, in galena, or lead ore, sulphur is a mineralizer;
   in hematite, oxygen is a mineralizer.

modded.en:
past participle of mod
n. a British teenager or young adult in the 1960s; noted for their clothes consciousness and opposition to the rockers
s. relating to a recently developed fashion or style;

modding.en:
-ing form of mod
n. a British teenager or young adult in the 1960s; noted for their clothes consciousness and opposition to the rockers
s. relating to a recently developed fashion or style;

monopetalous.en:
a. Having only one petal, or the corolla in one piece,
   or composed of petals cohering so as to form a tube or bowl;
   gamopetalous.

monophthong.en:
n. A single uncompounded vowel sound.
n. A combination of two written vowels pronounced as one;
   a digraph.

mucific.en:
a. Inducing or stimulating the secretion of mucus;
   blennogenous.
a. Secreting mucus.

multivocal.en:
a. Signifying many different things; of manifold meaning;
   equivocal.
n. A multivocal word.

musing.en:
n a calm, lengthy, intent consideration
v reflect deeply on a subject
s deeply or seriously thoughtful;
